GOTCHAS = [
 ("Reservations drop on a schedule.", "Most Resy restaurants release 30 days out at 9 or 10am ET; Tock tables (minibar, Jônt, Pineapple & Pearls, Kinship/Métier, Nakazawa) go in blocks — set Notify. Rose's Luxury and Little Pearl hold bar seats for walk-ins; arrive at 5:00 for a 5:30 opening. The Inn at Little Washington is a Resy Global Dining Access restaurant — your Platinum card gets you tables the public can't see."),
 ("Cash still matters at the counters.", "Ben's Chili Bowl, Horace & Dickie's, the Fish Market, Market Lunch, La Tejana and most of Eden Center are fastest or only in cash. Carry $60 in small bills on the neighborhoods day."),
 ("Tip 20%; check for the service charge.", "DC's tipped minimum wage has been rising under Initiative 82 and many restaurants now add a 3–20% service or 'I-82' charge — it's disclosed on the menu, and it is not the tip. Read the bill before adding 20% on top. Sales tax on meals is 10%."),
 ("The Metro is good, and it closes.", "Tap in with a contactless card or phone (SmarTrip is optional now). Trains run until midnight Sunday–Thursday and 1am Friday–Saturday; after that it's a car. Georgetown has no Metro station — walk from Foggy Bottom or take the Circulator."),
 ("Security and dress codes.", "The Capitol, the White House area and the museums are all bag-check; a small bag saves time. Off the Record, Round Robin and Quill don't enforce dress codes, but this is the most suit-wearing city in America and you'll feel it. Café Milano and the Waldorf expect an effort."),
 ("Monday is the dark day.", "Most starred restaurants close Sunday and/or Monday — minibar, Jônt, Rose's, Pineapple & Pearls, The Dabney all do. Bars and the Ethiopian restaurants run seven days. Rooftops are seasonal; The Wharf's stay open into November with heaters."),
 ("Museums are free; their cafés aren't secret anymore.", "Sweet Home Café at NMAAHC and Mitsitam at the American Indian museum are on this list on merit. The museum itself is free, but NMAAHC needs a timed pass — reserve online, or try the 8:15am same-day release."),
 ("The two cafeterias.", "Anyone can eat at the Longworth House Office Building cafeteria (through security) and the Supreme Court cafeteria when the Court isn't sitting. Cheap, decent, and full of the people who run the country."),
 ("Use the Amex credit like a local.", "Platinum: $100 per quarter; Gold: $50 twice a year. Pay with the enrolled card at any Resy or Tock venue showing the 'Resy Credit eligible' badge — no booking through Resy required. Check the quarter before the splurge night."),
 ("Anything marked verify, verify.", "DC lost a record ~100 restaurants in 2025 and the churn continued into 2026 — Cranes, Reverie and Tail Up Goat among them. Thirty seconds on Resy or Google before you cross town."),
 ("Half-smoke, mumbo sauce, jumbo slice.", "The half-smoke is a spiced pork-and-beef sausage — order it 'all the way' (chili, mustard, onions). Mumbo sauce is DC's sweet-tangy wing sauce, born in the carry-outs. The jumbo slice is an Adams Morgan 2am institution; it is not good, and that's not the point."),
 ("One for the road.", "Union Station has Pearl's Bagels and a Blue Bottle; National airport has a Ben's Chili Bowl. Dulles has nothing on this list — eat before you go."),
]
